From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 06:19:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] plugin_api: add Host API 3 pixel plugins

Host API 3 lets a generic plugin draw its own pixels. The plugin gets a
sealed memfd of frame slots on fd 3 (AERA_SURFACE_FD) and a SURFACE
message with its size, presents slots with PRESENT and gets them back
with FRAME_DONE; touches, keys and the keyboard come over the existing
control socket. A plugin opts in with protocol_version 3 and the
pixel-surface permission in its manifest, and gets a private data
directory (AERA_PLUGIN_DATA) that survives updates and goes with the
plugin.

The pixel plugin scene shows it full screen. It keeps a plugin running
across a rotation (a new SURFACE on the same memfd), pauses it when its
scene is left and resumes it from Recents, tells it AERA's light or dark
appearance, lets it pick files through the shared file picker, and lets
taps near the side edges reach it unless they swipe inward. The RPC can
open an installed plugin (op plugin, action open) for debugging over adb.
Tests and the Host API 3 section of plugin_api/README.md are included.

Squashed from p0g-stack/flutter-aera third_party/aera/patches 0001-0009,
0015, 0019-0022 and 0029; it needs the shared file picker (0018) first.
